; Two questions in one run.
;
; 1. What do the commands actually look like? Every long invocation so far was
;    test scaffolding: --root to keep tests off the real package root, --index
;    from before the index was published, --run-id/--report/--expect for the
;    evidence rule, --interrupt-at/--fail-at for fault injection. None of it is
;    needed to use pkg. Here it is with no flags at all, from C:.
;
; 2. Is a program built for mainline TODAY affected? abitest was compiled with
;    the current mainline SDK and calls exactly what the two archive binaries
;    died in: FindTask, then OpenLibrary of the same GUI libraries, then it
;    opens a window.

FAILAT 21

Echo "== 1. the commands, with nothing added =="
Copy "Qemu Vvfat:apkg" C:
Protect C:apkg +e

apkg update
apkg search zaphod
apkg install zaphod
apkg list
apkg remove zaphod

Echo "*N== 2. a program built for mainline today =="
Copy "Qemu Vvfat:abitest" RAM:
Protect RAM:abitest +e
RAM:abitest
Echo "== end =="
